WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.780
Pull up a chair. This is Models and Agents, Episode 60 on May 26th, 2026.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.140
Let's see what shipped. Let's see what happened in the AI world today, and trust me,

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.960
it's been busy. Local builders can now treat markdown skill files as

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.880
optimizable parameters with automated validation gates instead of manual tweaking.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.040
A new paper formalizes skill opt as a method that uses frontier models to

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:32.300
propose bounded edits to those markdown skills. Only edits that improve a held out validation set

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:38.960
are accepted. The best skills converge after 1-4 accepted edits and an edit budget of 4-8

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:45.820
works best while removing the cap collapses performance. A skill optimized on Codex transferred

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:54.280
directly to Cloud Code and gained 59.7 on spreadsheet bench. GPT 4.1 nano with an optimized skill

00:00:54.280 --> 00:01:00.140
roughly matched frontier performance on procedural tasks. The approach needs an auto-grader

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.740
with clear correct answers, which limits it to code and spreadsheets for now.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.480
Watch for follow-up work that relaxes the auto-grader requirement.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:17.560
The 35-billion-parameter TWEN variant now ships in an uncensored heretic configuration that

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:27.780
preserves all 785 MTPs. The 35-billion and 27-billion versions show KL divergences of 0.0487

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:38.580
and 0.0308 with accuracy losses of only 0.40% and 0.35%. The release includes safe tensors,

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:48.460
GGUF, NVFP4, and GPTQ in 4 formats. The author notes the 35-billion model targets general

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:56.280
purpose use while the 36-billion version focuses on agentic and coding tasks. Builders wanting an

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:03.360
uncensored general purpose model with preserved thinking tokens should test the Q4 or Q6 GGUF

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:10.560
experience. Ron's speech turns a pre-trained LLM into a speech LM through speech module alignment,

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:16.220
end-to-end pre-training with knowledge distillation, and multitask preference optimization.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:23.900
Training used 1.38 million hours of English and Korean data. The model tops 8 similarly sized

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:30.540
audio foundation models across 42 English and Korean speech and text benchmarks while keeping strong

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:37.800
text QA performance. Ron's speech chat adds full duplex conversation after continual training on

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:45.060
119,000 hours of dialogue data. Teams needing bilingual speech understanding and generation should

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:52.660
evaluate the open-sourced checkpoints. A new pull request adds support for TALKY 1930-13B

00:02:52.660 --> 00:03:00.360
hyphen IT inside the server backend. The 13-billion instruction-tune model was trained only on

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:07.980
pre-1931 English text and further aligned with online DPO. It enables historical roleplay

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:13.600
without modern knowledge contamination. Reference code and the hugging-face repo appear in the pull

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:19.160
request. Developers building vintage language or time period simulation agents now have

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:25.660
already to run 13-billion option. Shard delivers a drop-in hugging-face cache that reduces lab

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:34.180
math 3.18 billion KV memory by roughly 10 times at 8,000 context and 11 times at 32,000 context.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:42.080
It applies PCA plus int4 quantization to K after undoing rope and Hadamard rotation plus vector

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:48.420
quantization to V. Attention runs directly on the compressed keys with no measurable degradation

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:57.020
on Neahyath or Longbench. The repository sits at Krish 1905 slash Shard. Teams running long

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:02.900
context local inference should benchmark Shard against their current KV setup. A detailed thread

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:08.820
examines how local users test prompt injection and jailbreak resistance before wiring models to

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:15.780
tools, files, drag, shell commands, or browser automation. Most current setups focus on quantization,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:21.260
context length, and tokens per second while giving less attention to isolating tool access or

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:27.740
logging calls. Builders moving local models into agentic workflows should adopt the read-only

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:33.700
default and tool-call logging patterns raised in the thread. Gartner warns that applying uniform

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:40.780
governance across all enterprise AI agents is a death sentence. The report recommends differentiated

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:47.280
policies based on agent autonomy and risk. One size fits all controls will slow adoption without

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:53.900
improving safety. Enterprise teams evaluating agent platforms should review the governance segmentation

00:04:53.900 --> 00:05:00.160
guidance before standardizing policies. An article outlines the primary production failure modes

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:06.900
for agents and the first fixes teams should apply. It focuses on concrete engineering gaps rather

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:13.020
than high-level strategy. Developers shipping agents should read the prioritized fix list before

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:20.760
their next deployment review. A user measured real-world ASR performance on an Intel Arrow Lake NPU versus

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:29.820
CPU. The NPU delivered 2.8 to 6.1 times speed-ups and 10 to 21 times lower energy for 10 to 60 second

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:40.020
audio clips. The setup also frees VRAM on a 7,900 XTX and beats a previous 3060 EGPU for short

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:48.060
smart home voice commands. The Wyoming parakeet on Intel NPU repository is linked. Home assistant

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:55.780
or local voice developers should test the NPU path for always on ASR workloads. A post explains

00:05:55.780 --> 00:06:02.580
how context is divided across parallel slots and asks about consequences of exceeding model max

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:09.820
context or running two agents in parallel when VRAM allows. Practical questions cover performance,

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:17.340
energy, and slot allocation. Anyone moving from LM studio to the server back end for multi-agent setups

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.880
should review the flag interaction details. A step-by-step guide walks through loading the

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:30.820
Turing Enterprises slash open-MM-RL dataset, building a reward function that checks exact matches

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:38.820
and exporting for GRPO. It covers schema inspection, domain analysis, and vision language prompting.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:45.160
Developers starting multimodal reasoning projects with verifiable rewards can follow the pipeline

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:52.000
directly. A detailed post lists nine concrete changes that eliminated crashes and delivered 49

00:06:52.000 --> 00:07:00.660
to 65 tokens per second generation on a 14-inch M2 max. The changes include a 60Hz refresh rate,

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:08.640
GGUF over MLX, wired memory limit, preserve thinking flag, open code instead of cloud code,

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:17.640
and Q8KV cache minimum. The author shares exact fan curves and IO GPU wired limit meter settings.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:24.420
Mac users struggling with long agentic sessions should apply the refresh rate and memory limit steps

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:31.680
first. Okay, let's pop the hood on the NPU results. Everyone treats NPUs as marketing gimmicks for

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:37.760
LLMs. Yet the real engineering story is about power state transitions rather than raw tops.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:45.300
An NPU can exit deep sleep and begin useful work in a few milliseconds while a discrete GPU must

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:51.720
ramp clocks, allocate buffers, and warm PCIe links. This difference only matters for short,

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:58.340
bursty workloads. Once the task exceeds a few seconds, the GPUs higher sustained throughput wins.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:06.780
In the measured ASR case, the NPU delivered 4.8 times lower latency and 10.7 times less energy

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:13.780
on 10 second clips precisely because it avoided the GPU's ramp up tax. The practical decision rule

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:19.840
is simple. If average inference length is under roughly three seconds and you already have an NPU

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:26.800
in the SOC, root the work there. Anything longer or batch oriented still belongs on the GPU.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:32.600
The gotcha most teams miss is that the NPU's advantage disappears the moment you add a second

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:39.700
concurrent stream because its limited 13 tops cannot hide behind parallelism the way a larger GPU can.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:45.920
Test the skill opt edit and validate loop on a code or spreadsheet agent you already maintain.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:52.980
The 1-4 edit convergence pattern is worth reproducing. Run the 35 billion parameter

00:08:52.980 --> 00:09:00.680
uncensored heretic GGUF on your preferred back end and compare tool call stability with and without

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:06.160
preserve thinking enabled. Measure your current server setup with the parallel and context flags

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:11.600
against the slot division behavior described in the thread before scaling to multiple agents.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:19.580
Try the Wyoming Parakeet on Intel-NPU setup on any arrow lake machine you have for short voice

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:26.900
commands. The energy numbers are worth verifying locally. Apply the 60 hertz refresh rate and wired memory

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:32.980
limit changes on any MacBook running long context sessions and remeasure prompt processing time.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:41.220
More consumer hardware diffusion LLM training runs are expected following the open DLLM and D3 LLM

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:47.560
code drops. Additional server backend pull requests for historical and vintage models will likely land

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:55.260
as the talky-1930 effort gains visibility. Follow up work on validation gated skill optimization

00:09:55.260 --> 00:10:02.200
is anticipated. Once more teams reproduce the auto greater requirement. Tomorrow keep an eye on

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:09.160
expanded NPU integration examples for non-ASR workloads as the Intel arrow lake results circulate.

